menu "Muse hub (Even AI endpoint)"

    config HUB_HTTP_PORT
        int "HTTP port"
        default 8787

    config HUB_RELAY_TOKEN
        string "Bearer token, 32+ characters (set it in hub/sdkconfig.local)"
        default ""
        help
            Even AI sends it as "Authorization: Bearer <token>". The HTTP
            server does not start with a shorter one.

    config HUB_MDNS_NAME
        string "mDNS host name (<name>.local)"
        default "muse-hub"

    config HUB_WAIT_S
        int "Seconds a request waits for Muse's reply"
        default 25
        help
            Even AI gives up after about 30 s. A reply that takes longer is
            held; saying 「続き」 (or 「終わりまで」) returns it, any other
            prompt drops it and asks Muse anew.

    config HUB_MAX_CHARS
        int "Characters per page of a reply"
        default 2000
        range 100 5000
        help
            The G2 scrolls. A longer reply is split into pages; saying
            "続き" returns the next one.

    config HUB_ALL_MAX_CHARS
        int "Characters returned at once for the rest of a reply"
        default 5000
        range 300 5000
        help
            Characters returned at once for 「終わりまで」/「全部」; the G2 scrolls.

    config HUB_SIDE_CHAT
        bool "Send the gadget's turns to a Muse side chat"
        depends on MUSE_HATCH
        default n
        help
            Every turn (from the G2 and spoken on the StickS3) goes to one
            side chat of Muse instead of the main chat, and replies are read
            from it. Off: the main chat, as before.

    config HUB_SIDE_CHAT_ID
        string "Side chat ID (a lowercase UUID; empty: make one and keep it in NVS)"
        depends on HUB_SIDE_CHAT
        default ""
        help
            A side chat Muse already has, or a new UUID (the first message
            creates the chat). Empty: the hub makes one on first boot and
            keeps it in NVS (a full flash erase makes a new one).

endmenu
